<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $451 mln Dec 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $451 mln Dec 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $451 million surplus on December 18 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>Wednesday's surplus was due to an increase in financial buy transactions, which jumped to $1.193 billion, following the privatization of a branch of Brazil's federal railway network and the sale of a stake in southern telecoms.</p>
<p>Traders said Eurobond issues also contributed to bring more money in.  </p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 18</p>
<p>Exports: $216 million</p>
<p>Imports: $329 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.193 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $629 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $451 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.616 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.705 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.460 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.783 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.588 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
</text>
